# PPM (Netpbm): P3 (plain ASCII) and P6 (raw binary) rasters, 8-bit and
# 16-bit big-endian samples, header comments, and the whitespace rule that
# a comment counts as whitespace anywhere one is legal.
#
# The raster has to have exactly width * height * samples-per-pixel items, and a
# constraint on a repetition that has to be found by search takes very long for some
# seeds. So there is one alternative for each size (1 to 8 by 1 to 8), with the
# width, the height and the number of items written in it.

<start> ::= <p6_8> | <p6_16> | <p3>

